<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iraghticonnor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iraghticonnor, from the Irish Oireacht Uí Chonchúir, &quot;the inheritance of O'Connor&quot;, is a barony in north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-kerry">County Kerry</a>, Ireland, lying between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-feale">River Feale</a> and the Shannon estuary. It preserves the name of the territory held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oconnor-kerry">O'Connor Kerry</a> after the Anglo-Norman advance of the 13th century, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrigafoyle-castle">Carrigafoyle Castle</a> until the late 16th century. Its main town is Listowel.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iraghticonnor.jpg" alt="Iraghticonnor" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rauenstein · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lisselton,_Saint_Teresa%27s_Church.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
